# EtTooltip Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtTooltip` is a convenience wrapper around `EtBottomSheetV2` that provides a standardized pattern for displaying contextual information. It provides:

- **Title + close button header**: Left-aligned `heading-large` title with close button via `EtBottomSheet.Header.Action`
- **Body text content**: String children auto-wrapped in styled `EtText`
- **Compound component pattern**: `EtTooltip.Title` and `EtTooltip.Body` subcomponents
- **Imperative ref API**: `present()` / `dismiss()` via `EtTooltipRef` — no `BottomSheetModal` leak
- **Minimal boilerplate**: Replaces ~20 lines of `EtBottomSheetV2` + header setup

**Does NOT handle:**

- Complex interactive forms (use `EtBottomSheetV2` directly)
- Floating tooltip/popover positioning (use `EtPopover`)
- Custom header layouts beyond title + close (use `EtBottomSheetV2.Header` with compound subcomponents)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtTooltip` (main component)

```tsx
const tooltipRef = useRef<EtTooltipRef>(null);

<EtTooltip
  ref={tooltipRef}              // imperative handle: present() / dismiss()
  title?: string                // shorthand for EtTooltip.Title
  onClose?: () => void          // called when tooltip is dismissed (any path)
  testID?: string               // default: 'et-tooltip'
  accessibilityLabel?: string   // defaults to resolved title
  closeButtonAccessibilityLabel?: string  // default: 'Close'
>
  {children}
</EtTooltip>
```

### `EtTooltipRef` (imperative handle)

```tsx
interface EtTooltipRef {
  present: () => void;
  dismiss: () => void;
}
```

### `EtTooltip.Title` (title slot)

```tsx
<EtTooltip.Title
  testID?: string           // optional test identifier
>
  {string}  // extracted by parent for Header.Title
</EtTooltip.Title>
```

### `EtTooltip.Body` (body content)

```tsx
<EtTooltip.Body
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  {string | ReactNode}  // string auto-wrapped in EtText body-base-regular
</EtTooltip.Body>
```

### Types

| Type                  | Description                                            |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| `EtTooltipRef`        | Imperative handle (`present`, `dismiss`)               |
| `EtTooltipProps`      | Main component props                                   |
| `TooltipTitleProps`   | Title subcomponent props (`children: string`)          |
| `TooltipBodyProps`    | Body subcomponent props (`children: ReactNode`)        |
| `EtTooltipChildren`   | Valid children union (Title, Body, string)             |

## Usage Patterns

### Props-based API (simplest, recommended for most cases)

```tsx
const tooltipRef = useRef<EtTooltipRef>(null);

<EtTooltip ref={tooltipRef} title="Recently Traded">
  {t('recentlyTraded.disclaimer')}
</EtTooltip>
```

### Compound children API (for explicit structure)

```tsx
<EtTooltip ref={tooltipRef}>
  <EtTooltip.Title>Market Hours</EtTooltip.Title>
  <EtTooltip.Body>
    Trading hours vary by instrument.
  </EtTooltip.Body>
</EtTooltip>
```

### Custom rich body content

```tsx
<EtTooltip ref={tooltipRef} title="Risk Score">
  <EtTooltip.Body>
    <View style={{ gap: 12 }}>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">
        The risk score indicates volatility level.
      </EtText>
      <View style={styles.infoBox}>
        <EtText variant="body-secondary-semibold">
          1-3: Low | 4-6: Medium | 7-10: High
        </EtText>
      </View>
    </View>
  </EtTooltip.Body>
</EtTooltip>
```

### Typical info-icon integration

```tsx
function StatsHeader() {
  const tooltipRef = useRef<EtTooltipRef>(null);
  const { t } = useTranslation('stats');

  const handleInfoPress = useCallback(() => {
    tooltipRef.current?.present();
  }, []);

  return (
    <>
      <View style={styles.row}>
        <EtText variant="heading-base">{t('title')}</EtText>
        <EtIconV2 name="info-circle" size="sm" onPress={handleInfoPress} />
      </View>
      <EtTooltip ref={tooltipRef} title={t('title')}>
        {t('description')}
      </EtTooltip>
    </>
  );
}
```

## Anti-patterns

### Do NOT use for complex bottom sheets

```tsx
// BAD - EtTooltip is for simple info display
<EtTooltip ref={ref} title="Settings">
  <EtTooltip.Body>
    <TextInput value={name} onChangeText={setName} />
    <EtButton onPress={handleSave}>Save</EtButton>
  </EtTooltip.Body>
</EtTooltip>

// GOOD - use EtBottomSheetV2 directly for interactive content
<EtBottomSheetV2 bottomSheetRef={ref}>
  <EtBottomSheetV2.Header>
    <EtBottomSheetV2.Header.Title>Settings</EtBottomSheetV2.Header.Title>
    <EtBottomSheetV2.Header.Action onPress={handleClose} accessibilityLabel="Close">
      <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'close' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
    </EtBottomSheetV2.Header.Action>
  </EtBottomSheetV2.Header>
  <EtBottomSheetV2.Content>
    <TextInput value={name} onChangeText={setName} />
    <EtButton onPress={handleSave}>Save</EtButton>
  </EtBottomSheetV2.Content>
</EtBottomSheetV2>
```

### Do NOT use for floating tooltips

```tsx
// BAD - EtTooltip is a bottom sheet, not a floating overlay
<EtTooltip ref={ref} title="Hint">
  This appears next to the button
</EtTooltip>

// GOOD - use EtPopover for floating overlays
<EtPopover.Root visible={visible} popoverDirection="above">
  <EtPopover.Target>
    <Button />
  </EtPopover.Target>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Text>This appears next to the button</EtPopover.Text>
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

### Do NOT mix title prop with Title child

```tsx
// BAD - redundant, title prop takes precedence
<EtTooltip ref={ref} title="Prop Title">
  <EtTooltip.Title>Child Title</EtTooltip.Title>
  <EtTooltip.Body>Content</EtTooltip.Body>
</EtTooltip>

// GOOD - use one approach
<EtTooltip ref={ref} title="Title">
  Content
</EtTooltip>
```

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `EtBottomSheet` (from `bottom-sheet-v2`) - underlying bottom sheet
- `EtText` - text rendering for auto-wrapped body content
- `useEtoroTheme` - provides `textSecondaryNeutral` for body text color

### External Dependencies

- `@gorhom/bottom-sheet` - `BottomSheetModal` (internal, not exposed to consumers)
- `react-native` - `View`, basic primitives

### Design System Integration

- Title uses `heading-large` variant (left-aligned, per Figma)
- Body text uses `body-base-regular` variant with `textSecondaryNeutral` color
- Close button uses `close` icon at 24px via `EtBottomSheet.Header.Action`
- Spacing follows bottom sheet defaults (managed by `EtBottomSheetV2`)

